{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 42 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D2"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the clonazepam tablet shortage on 2023-03-10 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E11", "E5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortage lists six manufacturers including Accord Healthcare Inc., Aurobindo Pharma USA, Cheplapharm Arzneimittel GmbH, Prinston Pharmaceutical Inc., Rubicon Research Private Limited, and Teva Pharmaceuticals USA Inc.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E6", "E7", "E8", "E9", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A label for Northstar Rx LLC names Rubicon Research Limited (FEI 3008252295) as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1195651 at that plant ended 2023-01-27 and was classified VAI with the classification letter dated 2023-03-14, which is 42 days before the shortage posting on 2023-03-10.",
      "cites": ["E3", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An earlier FDA inspection 828916 at the same plant in 2013 was also classified VAI.",
      "cites": ["E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 246 tablets of the 1 mg presentation with 7.9 tablets used per day, giving 31.3 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-selected option is to buy from Advanced Rx Pharmacy of Tennessee LLC, which is not on FDA's shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    }
  ]
}
